From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joinery <joinery@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:01:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Make the Project Manager Joinery's, and ask what a project is
 made of

Two changes to the same screen.

Creating a project is when its founding decisions get made, so the dialog
walks steps: Godot's fields, the tools that will make it, then the art bible
in short themed pages. Next moves forward, Create finishes, and the title
says which step you are on. "Edit Now" appears only on the step that creates,
since it lives on the dialog root rather than inside a page.

Both questionnaires come from the `joinery` CLI, `tools --json` and
`bible --questions`, so the catalog and the bible's shape stay the one source
of truth. This code cannot invent a tool, offer one whose server is not
built, or decide what the bible asks or how it is grouped. Creating installs
the addon, runs `joinery setup` with the chosen tools, and hands the answers
to `joinery bible`, which renders them through templates/art_bible.md.

The Project Manager itself is stripped back to opening and creating. Gone are
the disk scan, the per-project sidebar, the view toggles, the asset store,
settings and donate: Joinery drives a project from the Journeyman sidebar once
one is open, so this screen only has to get you into one. The asset store in
particular is a place to download assets, which is the opposite of
creation-only. The logo becomes the name.

All of it hides rather than deletes. Upstream still constructs and refers to
those controls, and removing their construction is how a fork earns a null
dereference that compiles cleanly and crashes on launch. Hiding also means a
Godot release that moves things degrades into showing more UI, not breaking.

Typography follows the editor's theme: headings use its header variation,
question labels sit at body size, and guidance is dimmed but not shrunk.
Header variations are deliberately not used for guidance, since in this theme
they are larger than body text and invert the hierarchy.

Joinery-only, not for upstream: it reroutes stock flows into Joinery's own.
